Done — committed as `97283f9`.

**Change in `src/calculator.ts`:**
```ts
export function divide(a: number, b: number): number {
  if (b === 0) {
    throw new RangeError("Cannot divide by zero");
  }
  return a / b;
}
```
`b === 0` also catches `-0`, so `-Infinity` and `NaN` (`0/0`) cases are covered. `add` and `subtract` are untouched.

**Test:** I replaced the "deliberately absent" comment in `test/calculator.test.ts` with a case asserting `divide(1, 0)`, `divide(-1, 0)`, and `divide(0, 0)` all throw `RangeError`. `npm test` passes 4/4.

One note: `git add -A` also picked up an untracked `.claude/settings.json` (7 lines) that was sitting in the worktree — it wasn't part of my change. If it shouldn't be in the repo, `git rm --cached .claude/settings.json` and amend.
